positive_text:
Consider a sequence $ a_{1}, a_{2}, a_{3}, \ldots $ with $ a_{1} = 1 $. For any positive integer $ k $, the terms of the sequence are defined as follows:
$$
\begin{gathered}
a_{2k} = 
\begin{cases}
2 a_{k} & \text{if } k \text{ is even} \\
2 a_{k} + 1 & \text{if } k \text{ is odd}
\end{cases} \\
a_{2k+1} = 
\begin{cases}
2 a_{k} & \text{if } k \text{ is odd} \\
2 a_{k} + 1 & \text{if } k \text{ is even}
\end{cases}
\end{gathered}
$$
Prove that the sequence $ a_{1}, a_{2}, a_{3}, \ldots $ contains every positive integer exactly once.

negatives.text:
Let $ x_{1}, x_{2}, x_{3}, \ldots $ be a sequence such that $ x_{1} = 1 $ and, for $ k > 0 $, is defined by the relationship:
$$
\begin{gathered}
x_{2k} = 
\begin{cases}
2 x_{k} & \text{if } k \text{ is even} \\
2 x_{k} + 1 & \text{if } k \text{ is odd}
\end{cases} \\
x_{2k+1} = 
\begin{cases}
2 x_{k} & \text{if } k \text{ is odd} \\
2 x_{k} + 1 & \text{if } k \text{ is even}
\end{cases}
\end{gathered}
$$
Show that the sequence $ x_{1}, x_{2}, x_{3}, \ldots $ takes on every positive integer value more than once.

positive_text:
In triangle $\triangle ABC$, points $D$ and $E$ lie on sides $AB$ and $AC$, respectively, and point $F$ is on segment $DE$. Suppose $\frac{AD}{AB} = x$, $\frac{AE}{AC} = y$, and $\frac{DF}{DE} = z$. Show that

(1) the area of triangle $\triangle BDF$ is $(1-x)yz$ times the area of triangle $\triangle ABC$, and the area of triangle $\triangle CEF$ is $x(1-y)(1-z)$ times the area of triangle $\triangle ABC$;

(2) the sum of the cube roots of the areas of triangles $\triangle BDF$ and $\triangle CEF$ is less than or equal to the cube root of the area of triangle $\triangle ABC$.

negatives.text:
Let $\triangle ABC$ be a triangle. Points $D$ and $E$ are on sides $AB$ and $AC$, respectively, and point $F$ is on line segment $DE$. Let $\frac{AD}{AB} = x$, $\frac{AE}{AC} = y$, $\frac{EF}{DE} = z$. Prove that

(1) $S_{\triangle BDF} = (1-x)y(1-z)S_{\triangle ABC}$ and $S_{\triangle CEF} = x(1-y)zS_{\triangle ABC}$;

(2) $\sqrt[3]{S_{\triangle BDF}} + \sqrt[3]{S_{\triangle CEF}} \le \sqrt[3]{S_{\triangle ABC}}$.

Let $\triangle ABC$ be a triangle. Points $D$ and $E$ are on sides $AB$ and $AC$, respectively, and point $F$ is on line segment $DE$. Let $\frac{AD}{AB} = x$, $\frac{AE}{AC} = y$, $\frac{DF}{DE} = z$. Prove that

(1) $S_{\triangle BDF} = (1-x)y zS_{\triangle ABC}$ and $S_{\triangle CEF} = x(1-y)zS_{\triangle ABC}$;

(2) $\sqrt[3]{S_{\triangle BDF}} + \sqrt[3]{S_{\triangle CEF}} \le \sqrt[3]{S_{\triangle ABC}}$.

