Let $n > 1$ be an integer. Find all sequences $a_{1}, a_{2}, \ldots, a_{n^{2}+n}$ satisfying the following conditions:
(a) $a_{i} \in \{0,1\}$ for all $1 \leq i \leq n^{2}+n$;
(b) $a_{i+1}+a_{i+2}+\ldots+a_{i+n} = a_{i+n+1}+a_{i+n+2}+\ldots+a_{i+2n}$ for all $0 \leq i \leq n^{2}-n$.

Let $n > 1$ be an integer. Find all sequences $a_{1}, a_{2}, \ldots, a_{n^{2}+n}$ satisfying the following conditions:
(a) $a_{i} \in \{0,1\}$ for all $1 \leq i \leq n^{2}+n$;
(b) $a_{i+1}+a_{i+2}+\ldots+a_{i+n} > a_{i+n+1}+a_{i+n+2}+\ldots+a_{i+2n}$ for all $0 \leq i \leq n^{2}-n$.

positive_text:
Let $d(n)$ be the number of positive divisors of a natural number $n$. Find all functions $f: \mathbb{N} \rightarrow \mathbb{N}$ satisfying the following:
(1) For every natural number $x$, the number of positive divisors of $f(x)$ is exactly $x$;
(2) For all natural numbers $x$ and $y$, the value $f(x y)$ divides the expression $(x - 1) y^{x y - 1} f(x)$.

negatives.text:
For every $n \in \mathbb{N}$ let $d(n)$ denote the number of (positive) divisors of $n$. Find all functions $f: \mathbb{N} \rightarrow \mathbb{N}$ with the following properties:
(i) $d(f(x)) = x$ for all $x \in \mathbb{N}$;
(ii) $f(x y)$ divides $(x + 1) y^{x y - 1} f(x)$ for all $x, y \in \mathbb{N}$.

For every $n \in \mathbb{N}$ let $d(n)$ denote the number of (positive) divisors of $n$. Find all functions $f: \mathbb{N} \rightarrow \mathbb{N}$ with the following properties:
(i) $d(f(x)) = x$ for all $x \in \mathbb{N}$;
(ii) $f(x y)$ divides $(x - 1) y^{x y} f(x)$ for all $x, y \in \mathbb{N}$.

For every $n \in \mathbb{N}$ let $d(n)$ denote the number of (positive) divisors of $n$. Find all functions $f: \mathbb{N} \rightarrow \mathbb{N}$ with the following properties:
(i) $d(f(x)) = x + 1$ for all $x \in \mathbb{N}$;
(ii) $f(x y)$ divides $(x - 1) y^{x y - 1} f(x)$ for all $x, y \in \mathbb{N}$.

positive_text:
Consider two sequences $a_{n}$ and $b_{n}$ of whole numbers with the following rules:
(1) $a_{0}=0$, $b_{0}=8$;
(2) each next term follows $a_{n+2}=2 a_{n+1}-a_{n}+2$ and $b_{n+2}=2 b_{n+1}-b_{n}$;
(3) the sum of the squares $a_{n}^{2}+b_{n}^{2}$ is always a perfect square for $n>0$.
Find at least two possible values for the pair $\left(a_{1992}, b_{1992}\right)$.

negatives.text:
Consider a convex quadrilateral $ABCD$, in which $K, L, M, N$ are the midpoints of the sides $AB$, $BC$, $CD$, $DA$ respectively. Suppose
(a) $BD$ bisects $KM$ at $Q$;
(b) $QA = QB = QC$;
(c) $LK / LM = CD / CB$.
Prove that $ABCD$ is a square.

positive_text:
Consider a triangle $ABC$ with sides $a = BC$, $b = CA$, and $c = AB$. Let $R$ be the circumradius of the triangle, and let $r_a$, $r_b$, and $r_c$ be the exradii opposite to angles $A$, $B$, and $C$, respectively. Given that $2R \leq r_a$, show that:
(i) $a > b$ and $a > c$;
(ii) $2R > r_b$ and $2R > r_c$.

negatives.text:
Let $R$ denote the circumradius of a triangle $ABC$; $a, b, c$ its sides $BC, CA, AB$; and $r_{a}, r_{b}, r_{c}$ its exradii opposite $A, B, C$. If $2R \leq r_{a}$, prove that
(i) $b > a$ and $b > c$;
(ii) $2R > r_{b}$ and $2R > r_{c}$.

positive_text:
In a cyclic quadrilateral $ABCD$, the sides $AB$, $BC$, and $CD$ have lengths $a$, $b$, and $c$, respectively. It is given that $\angle ABC = 120^\circ$ and $\angle ABD = 30^\circ$. Show that
i) $c \geq a + b$;
ii) $|\sqrt{c+a} - \sqrt{c+b}| = \sqrt{c-a-b}$.

negatives.text:
In a cyclic quadrilateral $ABCD$, $AB = a$, $BC = b$, $CD = c$, $\angle ABC = 60^\circ$, and $\angle ABD = 30^\circ$. Prove that
i) $c \geq a + b$;
ii) $|\sqrt{c+a} - \sqrt{c+b}| = \sqrt{c-a-b}$.

positive_text:
Consider a function $ f $ from the set $ \{(x, y): x, y $ are real numbers with $ x y \neq 0\} $ into the set of all positive real numbers satisfying the following rules:
(1) $ f(x y, z) = f(x, z) f(y, z) $, for all $ x, y \neq 0 $;
(2) $ f(x, y z) = f(x, y) f(x, z) $, for all $ x, y \neq 0 $;
(3) $ f(x, 1 - x) = 1 $, for all $ x \neq 0, 1 $.
Prove that
(a) $ f(x, x) = f(x, -x) = 1 $, for all $ x \neq 0 $;
(b) $ f(x, y) f(y, x) = 1 $, for all $ x, y \neq 0 $.

negatives.text:
