a) $n=5$;

b) $n=6$?

A group of $n$ children each has a unique toy. They take turns trading toys: in each trade, two children exchange the toys they are holding at that moment. Every pair of children must trade at least once. After all the trades, each child ends up with the toy they started with, but one pair of children must trade an extra time for some reason. What is the minimum number of trades required, if:

a) $n=5$;

b) $n=6$?

A group of $n$ children each has a unique toy. They take turns trading toys: in each trade, two children exchange the toys they are holding at that moment. Each pair of children must trade at least once, and the number of trades must be even. After all the trades, each child ends up with the same toy they started with. What is the minimum number of trades required, if:

