positive_text:
Find all surjective functions $f: \mathbb{N} \rightarrow \mathbb{N}$ such that for any two positive integers $a$ and $b$, exactly one of the following is true:
$$
\begin{aligned}
f(a) &= f(b) \\
f(a + b) &= \min\{f(a), f(b)\}
\end{aligned}
$$

(Note: $\mathbb{N}$ is the set of all positive integers, and a function $f$ is surjective if every natural number appears as the output of $f$ for some input.)

negatives.text:
Find all surjective functions $f: \mathbb{N} \rightarrow \mathbb{N}$ such that for all positive integers $a$ and $b$, exactly one of the following equations is true:
$$
\begin{aligned}
f(a) &= f(b) \\
f(a + b) &= \max\{f(a), f(b)\}
\end{aligned}
$$

Find all surjective functions $f: \mathbb{N} \rightarrow \mathbb{N}$ such that for all positive integers $a$ and $b$, exactly one of the following equations is true:
$$
\begin{aligned}
f(a) &= f(b) \\
f(a - b) &= \min\{f(a), f(b)\}
\end{aligned}
$$

Find all surjective functions $f: \mathbb{N} \rightarrow \mathbb{N}$ such that for all positive integers $a$ and $b$, both of the following equations are true:
$$
\begin{aligned}
f(a) &= f(b) \\
f(a + b) &= \min\{f(a), f(b)\}
\end{aligned}
$$

positive_text:
\begin{enumerate}
\item For any integers $x, y$, and $z$, if $x + y\sqrt{2} + z\sqrt{3} = 0$, then prove that $x = y = z = 0$.
\item For any integers $p, q, r$, and $s$, if the expression $\frac{p + q\sqrt{2} + r\sqrt{3}}{q + r\sqrt{2} + s\sqrt{3}}$ is a rational number, then prove that $ps = qr$.
\end{enumerate}

negatives.text:
\begin{enumerate}
\item For all integers $s, t$, and $r$, if $s + \sqrt{2} t + \sqrt{3} r = 0$, then prove that $s + t + r = 0$.
\item For all integers $a, b, c$, and $d$, if the ratio $\frac{a + \sqrt{2} b + \sqrt{3} c}{b + \sqrt{2} c + \sqrt{3} d}$ is a rational number, then prove that $a + d = b + c$.
\end{enumerate}

\begin{enumerate}
\item For all integers $s, t$, and $r$, if $s + \sqrt{2} t + \sqrt{3} r = 0$, then prove that $s^2 + t^2 + r^2 = 0$.
\item For all integers $a, b, c$, and $d$, if the ratio $\frac{a + \sqrt{2} b + \sqrt{3} c}{b + \sqrt{2} c + \sqrt{3} d}$ is a rational number, then prove that $a^2 + d^2 = b^2 + c^2$.
\end{enumerate}

positive_text:
