positive_text:
Find the digits $A$, $B$, and $C$ such that the following multiplication works out correctly: 
$$
\begin{array}{c}
\overline{ABC} \cdot \overline{BAC} \\
\multicolumn{2}{c}{---} \\
--A & \\
\multicolumn{2}{c}{---B}
\end{array}
$$
We are told: $\overline{ABC} \cdot C$ ends with digit $A$, $\overline{ABC} \cdot A$ also ends with digit $A$, and $\overline{ABC} \cdot B$ ends with digit $B$. Each letter represents a different digit from 0 to 9, and each "-" represents a single unknown digit.

negatives.text:
