Let $ n $ be an integer with $ n \ge 3 $. Suppose there are $ n $ real numbers $ a_1, a_2, \dots, a_n $ such that:

i/  $ a_1 \ge a_2 \ge \dots \ge a_n $;
ii/  $ a_1 + a_2 + \dots + a_n = 0 $;
iii/  $ a_1^2 + a_2^2 + \dots + a_n^2 = n(n-1) $.

Determine the largest and smallest possible values of the sum $ T = a_1 + a_2 $.

